hyprland (0.55.0+ds-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  Starting from this upstream release, Hyprland supports Lua-based
  configuration as a replacement for the legacy hyprlang (.conf) syntax.
  If a hyprland.lua file is present, it will be loaded instead of
  hyprland.conf.

  Upstream has announced that the old hyprlang syntax will be supported
  for 1-2 more releases after 0.55, after which it will be dropped.
  Users are encouraged to migrate their configuration to Lua. Please
  refer to the upstream wiki at https://wiki.hypr.land for migration
  instructions.

 -- Carl Keinath <carl.keinath@gmail.com>  Wed, 20 May 2026 22:40:06 +0200
